<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan's HUBCO rises 1.25 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan's HUBCO rises 1.25 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Hub Power Co Ltd rose on Saturday following the announcement of the 1997/98 (July-June) budget which lowered wealth tax and gave incentives to boost the capital market, dealers said.</p>
<p>The power firm's 10-rupee stock rose 0.50 rupee, or 1.25 percent, to 40.65 on Saturday.</p>
<p>Some 61,000 shares were traded at the Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) which usually observes Saturday as a holiday. KSE has allowed special computerised trading a day after the budget.</p>
<p>Hubco, the largest private power plant in Pakistan, is expected to announce its first interim dividend in March 1998.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
